# Puzzle files are parsed by splitting on a bare CR: process_puzzle_file reads the intro and the
# floor encoding with read_lines(&file, ..., '\r') (puzzle.cpp). Git's line-ending normalisation
# would rewrite those terminators and the puzzle would fail to load -- and it fails as "Oh boy.
# Something is wrong with the puzzle file", which points at the content rather than at the
# checkout. Keep them byte-for-byte.
*.pzl -text

# Recorded demos and the packed art/resource archives are binary in every sense.
*.dmo -text
*.us1 -text
*.bmp -text
*.png -text
*.dat -text
